{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 1453.7, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "Validate prototype against real developer workflows; consider adding crates.io, Maven Central, Go pkg.go.dev; improve PyPI search via alternative API; add caching for repeated queries.", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "Built cross-platform need discovery prototype (E108) leveraging validated view-count principle across 5 platforms (PyPI, NPM, GitHub, NuGet, Hex.pm). Prototype 'needfind' takes natural language need descriptions, classifies them using E078/E103 framework, searches relevant platforms, ranks by view-count signal (downloads/stars), and outputs prioritized results. All 4 gates pass: G1 (5/5 test queries complete), G2 (results from 2+ platforms), G3 (need-related packages rank higher), G4 (cross-platform results combined). Key findings: NuGet shows massive download counts (billions for Microsoft packages), Hex.pm shows strong separation (jason 9.6M dl/30d), GitHub stars correctly rank major frameworks (Django 91k, FastAPI 103k). Limitation: GitHub API rate limiting (60/hr) affects detail enrichment; PyPI search blocked by JS challenge (using known package database as fallback).", "unlogged_changes": 1}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 14, "session": "2026-10-11-043-build-a-cross-platform-need-discovery-pr", "ts": "2026-10-11T19:05:18+00:00"}
